        solveit-data:techniqueDFT-1059 ;
    uco-core:name "Identify partitions" ;
    uco-action:endTime "2026-08-20T10:10:47.051979+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    uco-action:instrument kb:chain-tool-dissect-82ceb1bb-bc2b-5491-a96b-9889c336e40d ;
    uco-action:object kb:chain-output-bitstream-70645b64-b5ff-55d0-a0d7-6aedabd0fc7c ;
    uco-action:result kb:chain-output-partitions-78d18598-f945-5827-bd3a-314b35896e19 ;
    uco-core:description "Layer 2 of the web_search_history derivation: Identify partitions (DFT-1059). Tool(s) as run: dissect. dissect read the partition table opaquely. marple2's partition_table technique offers an independent pytsk3 reading of the same structures; running it is how an examiner would corroborate this layer." .

kb:chain-action-dft-1168-b9d5b4e3-16df-5a5d-a728-2049ec2b922e a case-investigation:InvestigativeAction,
        solveit-data:techniqueDFT-1168 ;
    uco-core:name "Identify volumes" ;
    uco-action:endTime "2026-08-20T10:10:47.051979+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    uco-action:instrument kb:chain-tool-dissect-82ceb1bb-bc2b-5491-a96b-9889c336e40d ;
    uco-action:object kb:chain-output-partitions-78d18598-f945-5827-bd3a-314b35896e19 ;
    uco-action:result kb:chain-output-filesystem-630e0d60-0a38-5f9a-845c-bb9261e3a104 ;
    uco-core:description "Layer 3 of the web_search_history derivation: Identify volumes (DFT-1168). Tool(s) as run: dissect. dissect mounted the volume opaquely. marple2 has no second implementation of volume identification — volume_ids is dissect-only — so this layer is single-implementation, not merely un-corroborated on this run." .

kb:chain-action-dft-1060-5080d9b3-4b5c-502c-9bb1-9990a50108b9 a case-investigation:InvestigativeAction,
        solveit-data:techniqueDFT-1060 ;
    uco-core:name "Enumerate files & folders" ;
    uco-action:endTime "2026-08-20T10:10:47.051979+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    uco-action:instrument kb:chain-tool-dissect-82ceb1bb-bc2b-5491-a96b-9889c336e40d ;
    uco-action:object kb:chain-output-filesystem-630e0d60-0a38-5f9a-845c-bb9261e3a104 ;
    uco-action:result kb:chain-output-file-set-efb494da-0857-5e39-9e6e-c55a24e2a449 ;
    uco-core:description "Layer 4 of the web_search_history derivation: Enumerate allocated files and folders (DFT-1060). Tool(s) as run: dissect. dissect's NTFS reader parsed the allocated filesystem structures, which is what lets the next layer resolve the browser's files by path. The FileSet this export carries is scoped to the files the later layers actually consumed, not to every file on the volume — the graph records the provenance of this result, not an inventory of the disk." .

kb:chain-action-dft-1169-db5dac3e-a520-5219-a82c-2b69b1de4078 a case-investigation:InvestigativeAction,
        solveit-data:techniqueDFT-1169 ;
    uco-core:name "Select the browser's files" ;
    uco-action:endTime "2026-08-20T10:10:47.051979+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    uco-action:instrument kb:chain-tool-dissect-82ceb1bb-bc2b-5491-a96b-9889c336e40d ;
    uco-action:object kb:chain-output-file-set-efb494da-0857-5e39-9e6e-c55a24e2a449 ;
    uco-action:result kb:chain-output-browserappfiles-13e2d8ef-f57c-5882-a444-a0d7587d4389 ;
    uco-core:description "Layer 5 of the web_search_history derivation: Filter files related to an application (DFT-1169). Tool(s) as run: dissect. dissect's browser plugin decides which files belong to a browser and where its profiles live. marple2 makes the same determination independently in browser_profiles and detected_browsers, from its own catalogue and from Local State / profiles.ini — a genuine second opinion on the selection, which did not run as part of this result. DFT-1169's declared output classes include BrowserAppFiles, so this is the step SOLVE-IT names between a FileSet and a browser extraction." .

kb:chain-action-dft-1137-f1c70193-7320-51cb-9946-8b44e1a16dee a case-investigation:InvestigativeAction,
        solveit-data:techniqueDFT-1137 ;
    uco-core:name "Parse browser history" ;
    uco-action:endTime "2026-08-20T10:10:47.051979+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    uco-action:instrument kb:chain-tool-dissect-82ceb1bb-bc2b-5491-a96b-9889c336e40d ;
    uco-action:object kb:chain-output-browserappfiles-13e2d8ef-f57c-5882-a444-a0d7587d4389 ;
    uco-action:result kb:chain-output-urlhistory-4387da19-1617-533f-a8be-bfd0a823f9a8 ;
    uco-core:description "Layer 6 of the web_search_history derivation: Extract browser history artifacts (DFT-1137). Tool(s) as run: dissect. dissect parsed the history store — Chrome's History SQLite, Firefox's places.sqlite, or the WebCacheV01.dat ESE database for Internet Explorer and Edge Legacy. marple2 has no independent history parser, so this layer is single-implementation. DFT-1137 takes BrowserAppFiles and produces URLHistory, exactly the arc drawn here." .

kb:chain-action-dft-1167-a5d945ed-b217-5106-856c-0ebf8ad9e132 a case-investigation:InvestigativeAction,
        solveit-data:techniqueDFT-1167 ;
    uco-core:name "Decode search terms from history URLs" ;
    uco-action:endTime "2026-08-20T10:10:47.051979+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    uco-action:instrument kb:chain-tool-marple2-00ede25d-7b17-55d7-abb6-dc14fee2a452 ;
    uco-action:object kb:chain-output-urlhistory-4387da19-1617-533f-a8be-bfd0a823f9a8 ;
    uco-action:result kb:chain-output-urlhistory-caa47c2e-8921-59b5-8bc0-7220ae9210bc ;
    uco-core:description "Layer 7 of the web_search_history derivation: Extract search terms from URLs (DFT-1167). Tool(s) as run: marple2. DFT-1167 is exactly this step — \"Parsing a URL and extracting search terms from the parameters\", with `q=` strings named in its details and Google and DuckDuckGo URLs as its examples — and its declared input, URLHistory, is precisely what DFT-1137 above produces, so the ladder joins without a gap. marple2's own _decode_search matches the URL host against a fixed list of search-engine suffixes and reads the query parameter each engine uses; that is marple2 logic, not a library's, so it is the same code whichever wrapper ran and cross-wrapper agreement on it would be vacuous. NOTE the output class here is marple2's reading, not the catalogue's: DFT-1167 declares uco-observable:keywordSearchTerm, a PROPERTY, because the technique yields a value rather than an object. A value cannot be an action's uco-action:result, so the layer's output is the narrowed URLHistory that carries that value on its entries — the smallest CASE object able to hold what the technique produces." .

